{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ענותו", :translit "anoto", :gloss "his affliction"} {:he "ב' במס'", :translit "bet be-masoret", :gloss "two in the Masorah"} {:he "ואידך גבי אמנון ותמר", :translit "ve-idach gabei amnon ve-tamar", :gloss "and the other concerning Amnon and Tamar"} {:he "מה התם בענין תשמיש", :translit "mah hetam be-inyan tashmish", :gloss "just as there in the matter of intimacy"} {:he "אף כאן היו מענים אותם", :translit "af kan hayu me'anim otam", :gloss "so here they were afflicting them"} {:he "כדי למעטן מתשמיש", :translit "kedei le-ma'atan mi-tashmish", :gloss "in order to diminish them from intimacy"} {:he "לבטלם מפריה ורביה", :translit "le-vatlam mi-periyah u-reviyah", :gloss "to prevent them from procreation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ענותו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking the root ע-נ-ה across contexts: intimacy in Amnon–Tamar and affliction in Egypt both curtailed through the same dynamic of coercion."}], :frame {:text "The root ע-נ-ה can carry the sense of intimate violation (Deuteronomy 22:24, II Samuel 13:14) or affliction (Exodus 1:11). Ba'al HaTurim reads the shared root as a hermeneutic link: the Egyptians afflicted the Israelites specifically to exhaust them and prevent marital relations, thwarting fulfillment of the commandment to be fruitful and multiply stated at Genesis 1:28. The midrashic tradition records that Pharaoh's intent behind the crushing labor was to break the Israelites' spirit and bodily capacity so they would not increase (Sotah 11b; Exodus Rabbah 1:10).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 22:24" "II Samuel 13:14" "Exodus 1:11" "Genesis 1:28" "Sotah 11b" "Exodus Rabbah 1:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "רעמסס", :translit "ra'mses", :gloss "Raamses"} {:he "ראשון מתרוסס", :translit "rishon mitroses", :gloss "the first one surges"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "רעמסס", :expansion ["ראשון מתרוסס"]} {:kind :other, :note "The word רעמסס is treated as a compound of ראשון ('first') and מתרוסס ('surges'), read letter-by-letter: ר-ע-מ / מ-ס-ס."}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ענותו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ענותו", :refs ["Psalms 132:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezerah shavah linking the root ע-נ-ה across contexts: intimacy in Amnon–Tamar and affliction in Egypt both curtailed through the same dynamic of coercion.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :notarikon, :word "רעמסס", :expansion ["ראשון מתרוסס"], :initials ["ר"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false} {:kind :other, :note "The word רעמסס is treated as a compound of ראשון ('first') and מתרוסס ('surges'), read letter-by-letter: ר-ע-מ / מ-ס-ס.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:13:04.231877791Z", :model "glm-5.2"}